course: dictionary
lesson: 3544
title: Feedback: using it to improve
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Feedback is information about how well you have done something, so you can do it better next time. Your teacher writes it on your work to show what went well and what to improve. «Your facts about lava were really clear» is useful feedback because it names one thing that works and says why.
explain: Feedback can also come from customers, who tell a company what they liked or disliked, or from players who tell a game maker what they think. A microphone can make feedback too, with a loud, high whistling squeal when it picks up the sound from its own speaker. In science, feedback is when the result of something goes back and changes what happens next.
explain: Useful feedback is kind, specific and helpful. «Good work» is kind but vague, while «Your ending made me want to read more» tells you exactly what worked. Peer feedback comes from a classmate and should work the same way. A low mark can feel unfair, but asking for feedback helps you see what to improve.
fact: Feedback is information about how well you did something, so you can do it better next time.
fact: Useful feedback names one thing that works and one clear thing to improve.
fact: «Give feedback» and «get feedback» are common phrases at school.
fact: «Constructive feedback» means helpful advice that aims to improve your work.
fact: In science, feedback is when a result goes back and changes what happens next.
exercise: Teacher writes «Your facts about lava were really clear.» What kind of feedback is this? | A new word for a volcano | A rule about spelling | A loud microphone squeal | *Useful feedback that names what works
exercise: A microphone picks up its own speaker and makes a loud, high squeal. What is this called? | A feedback form | *Feedback, as a whistling noise | Peer feedback | Customer feedback
exercise: Which comment is kind, specific and helpful? | Bad | Whatever | *Your ending made me want to read more | Good work
test: Your classmate reads your story and suggests improvements. What is this called? | Customer feedback | Science feedback | A microphone squeal | *Peer feedback
test: In science, what is feedback? | A kind of food | A loud squeal from a speaker | *A result that goes back and changes what happens next | A quiet, clean room
exam: Which comment gives feedback that is kind, specific and helpful? | *Your dialogue sounded natural and kept me reading | Mm, fine | Nice | Whatever you think
